xnu 0222: what a submission cleans and how often it looks at the fence

Three costs the submission path paid on every submission and does not need.

The ring clean. Every doorbell cleaned all 32 KiB of the CP ring -- 512 `dc
civac` lines, eight `pmap_find_phys` and eight `dsb sy` -- to publish the 104
bytes a submission writes, and a frame is five submissions. Only this path
writes the ring and each submission is cleaned when it is written, so the
range this submission wrote is the range that has to go out:
`mondrian_gpu_mem_flush_range` takes an offset, and it still splits at a 4 KiB
boundary because the next physical page is not contiguous with this one.
`gpuringslow=1` cleans the whole ring again: the valve for a boot where the CP
reads a ring dword the CPU never flushed, whose symptom is 0182's
unknown-opcode halt.

The backpressure read. CP_RB_RPTR was read before every submission: an
uncached round trip to the GPU, five a frame, always to learn that the ring
was empty. The pointer only moves forward inside a lap, so a value read once
stays a valid lower bound until the write position is a whole lap past it --
while (at - seen) mod size is under size - 26, the 26 dwords written next
cannot reach the CP whatever it does in between. The register is read once a
lap now (315 submissions of 26 dwords here) and whenever that bound expires;
the room test and its 2 s patience are unchanged.

The fence wait polled with `delay(1000)`. Nothing can wake it: the GPU's SPI
is masked in the distributor before the SQE starts (the ICENABLER9 write in
the bring-up) and no CP handler wakes a waiter, so the poll interval *is* the
resolution of every wait -- and each frame's glFinish, which waits for the
last submission's fence, paid up to a millisecond after the GPU was already
done. It is 100 us now, `gpuwaitpoll=US` (clamped to 10..1000) to move it back
to 1000, in `mondrian_gpu_uc_wait` and in the two waits inside the submit
path; every timeout is unchanged in wall time, because the loops count
microseconds instead of iterations. The old interval was also the measurement
quantum: every stream that completes on its own reports `uc big 71 dwords ...
in 1 ms`, which a 1 ms poll cannot resolve finer.

what the next boot's log says
	MONDRIAN GPU: uc ring 1024 submissions, N ns a clean, 26 of 8192 dwords
	a submission, M rptr reads
	    N against the 512 cache lines of the whole ring, and 26 of 8192 with
	    one read a lap, are the two halves of this change running; the same
	    boot with gpuringslow=1 says 8192 dwords and one read a submission.
	MONDRIAN GPU: uc fence N ... in X us, poll 100 us
	    X under a millisecond is a wait the old poll could not report.
	mondrian-gl: frame NNN: ... (X handing on, Y waiting, Z copying out)
	    "waiting" carries the glFinish, so it drops by the poll quantum;
	    "handing on" carries the submit, so it drops by four of the five
	    ring cleans and reads of a frame.
